From d2eb95995363e563fa14002fec569e635546ad60 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 13:02:35 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Validate local assembly with signed mature dependent payments

Reuse the existing explicit genesis/profile and immutable fork corpus. Fund a public scalar-3 CHECKSIGVERIFY policy through actual complete-block assembly and validation, mature its coinbase, then supply a signed parent and signed child in order. Compare an independent zero-claim quote with the final fixed-width claim, costs and monetary transition, mine within 256 attempts and require normal full validation plus actual runtime admission/retention/recovery/acknowledgement.

Verify raw logical database keys remain identical across previews, construction and typed failures. Exercise zero/capped/u64-maximum request claims, bad signatures, reversed order, stale parent, real J/R/P gates, canonical data and resource limits, and nonce refusal/exhaustion without wrap. Derive insufficient entitlement from the real encoded charge under the existing bare monetary schedule without reusing one-byte toy arithmetic or inventing funding.

Strict Debug passes against frozen preview core 7c8ced2fc and assembler/store wrapper 2350e1544. Commit only the four authorized assembler test/fixture/build/documentation files; borrowed runtime/core/store sources and shared CMake changes are excluded. A greater-than-u64 funded entitlement vector is not claimed.
